WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.299 --> 00:00:03.010
History is often the greatest teacher.

00:00:03.010 --> 00:00:07.790
By looking at the past, we can learn from
it with the benefit of hindsight.

00:00:07.790 --> 00:00:13.360
Such as in the early twentieth century, when
the entire planet was in the grip of a horrifying

00:00:13.360 --> 00:00:14.360
war.

00:00:14.360 --> 00:00:19.119
At the time, this conflict was often referred
to as The Great War, although there was little

00:00:19.119 --> 00:00:20.310
“great” about it.

00:00:20.310 --> 00:00:26.060
Others knew it as the War to End All Wars,
the largest armed engagement the world had

00:00:26.060 --> 00:00:28.880
known, although it would not be the last.

00:00:28.880 --> 00:00:34.310
Today, with that hindsight we just mentioned,
we know it as World War One.

00:00:34.310 --> 00:00:40.519
In June 1914, an Archduke of Austria was shot
dead by a Serbian assassin, and as a result

00:00:40.519 --> 00:00:45.440
of the complicated treaties forged between
various nations, soon much of the world was

00:00:45.440 --> 00:00:50.489
involved in a war that started out as little
more than a scuffle between neighbors.

00:00:50.489 --> 00:00:55.239
The horrors of trench warfare, the carnage
caused by the earliest chemical weapons and

00:00:55.239 --> 00:01:01.440
armored tanks, left a permanent and lasting
scar on the world’s history, one still mourned

00:01:01.440 --> 00:01:03.719
and remembered to this day.

00:01:03.719 --> 00:01:08.500
The advances in chemical and mechanized warfare
that took place during World War One ranged

00:01:08.500 --> 00:01:13.930
from the use of chemicals like tear gas used
to disable targets, to more lethal compounds

00:01:13.930 --> 00:01:15.760
like mustard gas.

00:01:15.760 --> 00:01:20.720
And of course, this was the first war to introduce
tanks to the battlefield.

00:01:20.720 --> 00:01:25.490
Although these were clumsy and cumbersome
to begin with, it was arguably the advent

00:01:25.490 --> 00:01:30.220
of the First World War that forced many advancements
in armored warfare.

00:01:30.220 --> 00:01:35.060
It was the belief of many intellectuals on
all sides that if the Great War was made too

00:01:35.060 --> 00:01:40.190
gruesome and horrific to continue, it would
come to its natural end.

00:01:40.190 --> 00:01:45.720
This, of course, did not happen, only encouraging
each participant of World War One to continue

00:01:45.720 --> 00:01:47.610
advancing their weaponry.

00:01:47.610 --> 00:01:52.660
But what if there were weapons developed during
World War One that were too dangerous to be

00:01:52.660 --> 00:01:53.660
deployed?

00:01:53.660 --> 00:01:58.290
With every side looking for any advantage
over their adversaries, what if some turned

00:01:58.290 --> 00:02:04.130
to the unethical, even the anomalous, to gain
the upper hand in the war?

00:02:04.130 --> 00:02:10.860
Introducing SCP-186, otherwise known as To
End All Wars.

00:02:10.860 --> 00:02:16.660
Try to imagine weaponry that was so incredibly
advanced for the mid-1910s, yet so horribly

00:02:16.660 --> 00:02:19.450
and unjustifiably cruel.

00:02:19.450 --> 00:02:24.500
Worse than gas that can cause blisters to
form not only on the skin but also inside

00:02:24.500 --> 00:02:26.000
the lungs.

00:02:26.000 --> 00:02:31.240
More advanced than armored vehicles with mounted
machine guns crawling across No Man’s Land.

00:02:31.240 --> 00:02:35.920
It’s hard to picture something that could
be more devastating than that, especially

00:02:35.920 --> 00:02:37.490
for the time period.

00:02:37.490 --> 00:02:42.050
But a good measure of a weapon’s destructive
power is usually found in the damage it leaves

00:02:42.050 --> 00:02:43.340
in its wake.

00:02:43.340 --> 00:02:51.130
In this case, SCP-186 is exactly that; not
the anomalous weapons themselves, but the

00:02:51.130 --> 00:02:58.310
site of a battle that took place between the
24th of July and the 13th of August in 1917.

00:02:58.310 --> 00:03:03.120
The event became known as the Battle of Husiatyn
Woods, but you won’t find any mention of

00:03:03.120 --> 00:03:04.959
it in the history books.

00:03:04.959 --> 00:03:10.180
Any and all records of the battle have been
secretly expunged by the SCP Foundation, and

00:03:10.180 --> 00:03:14.730
their own archive is now the only place where
someone can find details of what happened

00:03:14.730 --> 00:03:16.830
over those few weeks.

00:03:16.830 --> 00:03:21.970
The engagement took place between the German
Imperial Army and forces belonging to Russia’s

00:03:21.970 --> 00:03:26.720
provisional government, a small skirmish in
comparison to the enormity of many battles

00:03:26.720 --> 00:03:28.400
of the First World War.

00:03:28.400 --> 00:03:32.960
So, what happened at the Battle of Husiatyn
Woods to make it so horrible it had to be

00:03:32.960 --> 00:03:35.380
stricken from the historical record?

00:03:35.380 --> 00:03:40.820
For that we have to go back to Husiatyn, a
small settlement in western Ukraine, in July

00:03:40.820 --> 00:03:42.460
of 1917.

00:03:42.460 --> 00:03:45.950
The surviving remnants of a Russian division
had been scattered.

00:03:45.950 --> 00:03:50.390
The Germans’ counterattack against the Kerensky
Offensive had driven the Russian troops to

00:03:50.390 --> 00:03:53.959
the dense forest that surrounded the town
of Husiatyn.

00:03:53.959 --> 00:03:58.290
You might be forgiven for thinking that the
outnumbered Russian force was decimated by

00:03:58.290 --> 00:04:01.739
almost five hundred German soldiers pursuing
them.

00:04:01.739 --> 00:04:04.960
But you would be very, very wrong.

00:04:04.960 --> 00:04:09.900
As the opposing forces met, they engaged each
other in a fearsome battle.

00:04:09.900 --> 00:04:15.050
But this was unlike any encounter that had
taken place over the course of World War One,

00:04:15.050 --> 00:04:17.109
or ever would again.

00:04:17.109 --> 00:04:22.189
Both sides were armed with anomalous weaponry,
possessing technology beyond any that had

00:04:22.189 --> 00:04:24.250
ever been seen at the time.

00:04:24.250 --> 00:04:29.419
To this day, the SCP Foundation has been baffled
by these weapons.

00:04:29.419 --> 00:04:34.130
Even with their unique understanding of the
anomalous, Foundation researchers have been

00:04:34.130 --> 00:04:39.250
unable to replicate any of them, and instead
keeps them secured in the munitions wing of

00:04:39.250 --> 00:04:45.090
Site-23, all under the designation of SCP-186-1.

00:04:45.090 --> 00:04:52.999
Among the recovered instances of SCP-186-1
is a highly modified Skoda M1909 machine gun.

00:04:52.999 --> 00:04:58.240
However, rather than behaving like a standard
firearm, this gun would cause rapid forming

00:04:58.240 --> 00:05:02.800
growths, not unlike tumors, to appear within
the body of its targets.

00:05:02.800 --> 00:05:08.729
Another was concertina wire, a form of spiraled
razor wire commonly used in trenches.

00:05:08.729 --> 00:05:13.620
Only this wire was coated in an unknown compound
that caused permanent hallucination whenever

00:05:13.620 --> 00:05:18.120
the wire cut a person and allowed the hallucinogen
to enter their bloodstream.

00:05:18.120 --> 00:05:23.979
A number of rifle cartridges were also found
littered around SCP-186.

00:05:23.979 --> 00:05:27.300
Sounds pretty normal for a First World War
battlefield, right?

00:05:27.300 --> 00:05:31.949
Except these cartridges were not filled with
gunpowder like you would expect them to be.

00:05:31.949 --> 00:05:37.169
Instead, they inexplicably contained human
bone, ground into powder.

00:05:37.169 --> 00:05:42.020
The purpose of this ammunition, or how it
was manufactured, is still unknown to the

00:05:42.020 --> 00:05:43.800
SCP Foundation.

00:05:43.800 --> 00:05:49.690
As if a gun that causes tumors and hallucination-triggering
wire weren’t bad enough, Foundation researchers

00:05:49.690 --> 00:05:55.339
also found a number of grenades used by the
troops at the site of SCP-186.

00:05:55.339 --> 00:06:01.419
These were British Empire standard issue No.
27 grenades, but they contained a unique,

00:06:01.419 --> 00:06:05.939
anomalous gas that was capable of passing
through any and all filters.

00:06:05.939 --> 00:06:09.969
Gas masks were developed during World War
One to protect soldiers from mustard and tear

00:06:09.969 --> 00:06:16.330
gas on the battlefield, but these masks only
offered basic filtration by today’s standards.

00:06:16.330 --> 00:06:22.059
Even so, the gas contained in these grenades
was strong enough to negate any and all filtration

00:06:22.059 --> 00:06:25.970
systems, but that was far from its worst quality.

00:06:25.970 --> 00:06:28.409
Did this unknown gas choke troops?

00:06:28.409 --> 00:06:29.409
Not quite.

00:06:29.409 --> 00:06:31.719
Did it disable them like tear gas?

00:06:31.719 --> 00:06:38.449
In a way, yes, but this gas did so by making
any soldier exposed to it experience the sensation

00:06:38.449 --> 00:06:41.630
of having their body set on fire.

00:06:41.630 --> 00:06:42.869
Constantly.

00:06:42.869 --> 00:06:48.349
Also recovered at SCP-186 were the remains
of some form of explosive, and it is believed

00:06:48.349 --> 00:06:52.259
by the Foundation that this was detonated
at the culmination of the Battle of Husiatyn

00:06:52.259 --> 00:06:56.770
Woods, causing approximately a third of the
battle’s total casualties.

00:06:56.770 --> 00:07:01.389
Foundation researchers estimate that almost
three hundred civilians were either caught

00:07:01.389 --> 00:07:07.349
in the blast, or died as a result of the crossfire
between the German and Russian forces.

00:07:07.349 --> 00:07:14.129
The soldiers involved were all also permanently
incapacitated or killed, or at least, almost

00:07:14.129 --> 00:07:15.129
all of them.

00:07:15.129 --> 00:07:18.449
So, where did all these anomalous weapons
come from?

00:07:18.449 --> 00:07:23.169
And why were they used just in this battle,
not throughout the First World War?

00:07:23.169 --> 00:07:27.569
According to records kept from the public
by the SCP Foundation, the German troops in

00:07:27.569 --> 00:07:34.059
the Husiatyn Woods were accompanied by a Hungarian
advisor to their military named Mátyás Nemeş.

00:07:34.059 --> 00:07:38.369
Under his orders, they specifically targeted
and tracked the Russian division that was

00:07:38.369 --> 00:07:44.330
retreating from them, who were similarly accompanying
a French scientist, Dr. Jean Durand.

00:07:44.330 --> 00:07:49.689
It was these two men, Nemeş and Durand, who
were responsible for arming the Germans and

00:07:49.689 --> 00:07:53.149
Russians with their arsenals of anomalous
weapons.

00:07:53.149 --> 00:07:58.419
They had ensured that their inventions of
death had only received limited manufacturing,

00:07:58.419 --> 00:08:02.809
and had intentionally joined opposing sides
of the war effort to test their creations

00:08:02.809 --> 00:08:04.469
in real combat.

00:08:04.469 --> 00:08:08.999
In other words, it appears that Durand and
Nemeş had been working together since the

00:08:08.999 --> 00:08:13.979
beginning of the war, and the troops they
were with had been manipulated into taking

00:08:13.979 --> 00:08:16.389
part in a big test.

00:08:16.389 --> 00:08:20.669
These soldiers were just as unlucky as the
civilians caught in the crossfire.

00:08:20.669 --> 00:08:25.639
Today, the SCP Foundation has established
an automated security perimeter around the

00:08:25.639 --> 00:08:31.469
site of SCP-186, preventing access to anyone
unless authorized.

00:08:31.469 --> 00:08:36.810
Everything within the perimeter is frequently
patrolled and observed by security personnel.

00:08:36.810 --> 00:08:40.110
Why the need for so much security at an old
battleground?

00:08:40.110 --> 00:08:45.330
Given the damage caused by the use of so many
anomalous weapons, including those the Foundation

00:08:45.330 --> 00:08:52.220
were unable to recover, the area of SCP-186
has become a hotspot for unusual happenings,

00:08:52.220 --> 00:08:55.449
even long after the Battle of Husiatyn Woods
ended.

00:08:55.449 --> 00:08:59.480
These anomalies include abnormal environmental
or weather conditions.

00:08:59.480 --> 00:09:03.819
For example, all the trees in the southwestern
portion of the former battlefield died and

00:09:03.819 --> 00:09:09.279
decomposed at an accelerated rate in 1923,
while the temperature dropped to a permanent

00:09:09.279 --> 00:09:15.230
minus fifteen degrees Celsius four years later,
but yet there was never any snowfall.

00:09:15.230 --> 00:09:21.300
Then there were the sounds of gunfire in 1932,
despite there being nobody inside the SCP-186

00:09:21.300 --> 00:09:22.300
site.

00:09:22.300 --> 00:09:27.389
A number of years later, a pair of Foundation
agents disappeared on a routine patrol of

00:09:27.389 --> 00:09:30.520
the area, and were never seen again.

00:09:30.520 --> 00:09:36.269
Of course, 23 years after the end of the War
to End All Wars, the world was plunged into

00:09:36.269 --> 00:09:39.660
chaos and found itself at war once again.

00:09:39.660 --> 00:09:46.449
During this time, SCP Foundation personnel
were instructed to evacuate the site of SCP-186,

00:09:46.449 --> 00:09:51.320
based on intelligence from their allied operatives
who were working undercover inside the Third

00:09:51.320 --> 00:09:52.320
Reich.

00:09:52.320 --> 00:09:57.470
As the Foundation disembarked their observation
posts, a faint glow was visible coming from

00:09:57.470 --> 00:10:00.110
SCP-186.

00:10:00.110 --> 00:10:04.069
Four years passed, and the Second World War
came to a close.

00:10:04.069 --> 00:10:09.980
The Foundation returned to re-establish their
containment of SCP-186, and immediately discovered

00:10:09.980 --> 00:10:16.149
thirteen corpses dressed in German army uniforms,
bearing the insignia of the fourth Panzer

00:10:16.149 --> 00:10:17.250
Army.

00:10:17.250 --> 00:10:22.680
There were a further 27 bodies of soldiers
wearing the garb of the Soviet 22nd Army.

00:10:22.680 --> 00:10:28.110
Both sets of bodies had already begun decaying,
although someone had removed the dog tags

00:10:28.110 --> 00:10:32.060
and anything else that could identify these
dead troops.

00:10:32.060 --> 00:10:37.910
It seemed that history had, to some extent,
repeated itself, as the Nazi and Soviet forces

00:10:37.910 --> 00:10:42.060
had clashed on the same battlefield where
their German and Russian predecessors had

00:10:42.060 --> 00:10:45.639
fought during the Battle of Husiatyn Woods.

00:10:45.639 --> 00:10:52.350
Years later, in 1959, a large sinkhole formed
in the northeast portion of SCP-186.

00:10:52.350 --> 00:10:57.640
Four men were found wandering nearby, all
extremely disorientated, wearing decomposing

00:10:57.640 --> 00:10:59.050
military uniforms.

00:10:59.050 --> 00:11:02.850
Were they lost survivors of the Nazi-Soviet
battle?

00:11:02.850 --> 00:11:09.760
No, these men were in World War One uniforms,
German Empire and Russian standard issue.

00:11:09.760 --> 00:11:14.980
They had survived the Battle of Husiatyn Woods,
and were somehow still standing, even though

00:11:14.980 --> 00:11:18.300
they should have died during the First World
War.

00:11:18.300 --> 00:11:20.400
How did these troops manage this?

00:11:20.400 --> 00:11:26.360
Well, the final anomalous weapon recovered
at the site of SCP-186 were mortar shells,

00:11:26.360 --> 00:11:30.670
but unsurprisingly, these weren’t your standard
high explosive artillery.

00:11:30.670 --> 00:11:35.949
Much like those grenades mentioned earlier,
these mortar shells contained a unique, previously

00:11:35.949 --> 00:11:37.790
unseen gas.

00:11:37.790 --> 00:11:42.600
But instead of causing the perpetual pain
of being on fire, this gas altered the biology

00:11:42.600 --> 00:11:45.970
of cells that it came into contact with.

00:11:45.970 --> 00:11:51.160
Somehow, it triggered a change that prevented
a body’s cells from ceasing life function,

00:11:51.160 --> 00:11:53.920
keeping them continuously operational.

00:11:53.920 --> 00:11:58.790
In other words, it meant that any soldiers
exposed to the gas simply could not die.

00:11:58.790 --> 00:12:03.199
That’s right, some of the troops involved
in the Battle of Husiatyn Woods are still

00:12:03.199 --> 00:12:05.410
alive to this day.

00:12:05.410 --> 00:12:10.459
The SCP Foundation immediately began excavating
the sinkhole, and discovered twenty three

00:12:10.459 --> 00:12:13.160
bodies buried beneath in a mass grave.

00:12:13.160 --> 00:12:18.240
They were more of the surviving World War
One soldiers, kept alive for decades by the

00:12:18.240 --> 00:12:19.690
mortar gas.

00:12:19.690 --> 00:12:24.160
Some of them still had infected wounds and
battlefield injuries that should have killed

00:12:24.160 --> 00:12:27.350
them, yet their bodies refused to die.

00:12:27.350 --> 00:12:32.110
The soldiers were rounded up and hauled off
to Site-23, where the Foundation’s researchers

00:12:32.110 --> 00:12:33.829
began assessing them.

00:12:33.829 --> 00:12:38.629
However, they were unable to glean any useful
information from the German and Russian troops

00:12:38.629 --> 00:12:40.430
that had been unearthed.

00:12:40.430 --> 00:12:45.329
All of the soldiers exhibited symptoms of
extensive psychological trauma, and had developed

00:12:45.329 --> 00:12:49.460
various mental disorders while buried alive
under the battlefield.

00:12:49.460 --> 00:12:54.889
They had all been driven to insanity, perhaps
as a result of their unnaturally extended

00:12:54.889 --> 00:13:00.389
lifespans, maybe from being buried underground
and unable to die for so long.

00:13:00.389 --> 00:13:05.829
Or perhaps it was the wartime atrocities they
witnessed that drove the soldiers over the

00:13:05.829 --> 00:13:06.829
brink.

00:13:06.829 --> 00:13:08.220
History is a great teacher.

00:13:08.220 --> 00:13:12.670
But those willing to forget its mistakes are
often doomed to repeat them.

00:13:12.670 --> 00:13:20.050
Mátyás Nemeş and Dr. Jean Durand created
the anomalous weapons responsible for SCP-186,

00:13:20.050 --> 00:13:24.759
and similar minds would later go on to build
the atomic bomb and countless weapons of mass

00:13:24.759 --> 00:13:26.680
destruction after.

00:13:26.680 --> 00:13:32.110
World wars, the suffering of countless troops
and civilians, these parts of history mean

00:13:32.110 --> 00:13:37.420
nothing if we don’t allow ourselves to learn
from them, and maybe that’s our curse as

00:13:37.420 --> 00:13:45.010
a species, that we are doomed to fight the
war to end all wars again, and again, and

00:13:45.010 --> 00:13:46.010
again.

00:13:46.010 --> 00:13:53.161
Now check out “SCP-2273 - Major Alexei Belitrov”
and “SCP-1461 - House of the Worm” for

00:13:53.161 --> 00:13:55.419
more wild, war-related SCPs!

